.TH QUADRF-APPLY-WIFI 8 "August 2026" "QuadRF" "QuadRF"
.SH NAME
quadrf-apply-wifi \- provision a Wi-Fi network and reboot into it
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quadrf-apply-wifi
.I ssid
.RI [ passphrase ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Replaces
.I /etc/wpa_supplicant/wpa_supplicant.conf
with a single network for
.IR ssid ,
using
.I passphrase
for WPA or an open network when none is given, and reboots the appliance three
seconds later.
.PP
The reboot is detached so the caller can finish first: the web control panel
invokes this through the sudoers rule in
.I /etc/sudoers.d/quadrf
and needs to return its response before the system goes down.
.PP
Any previously configured network is discarded. If the new one does not
associate, the appliance comes back on its fallback access point; see
.BR quadrf-hotspot (8).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR quadrf (1),
.BR quadrf-hotspot (8),
.BR wpa_supplicant.conf (5)
